        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>Devil&#x27;s-self-elevation argument (vv. 9-12; expands seed 1:3 hubris-speech): the Devil&#x27;s reasoning for refusing to bow — claims of ontological-precedence (created first / created higher / created from purer matter). The pre-existence-from-purer-matter argument is the standard fall-of-Satan rationale in: VITA ADAE ET EVAE §§14-16 (Satan: &#x27;I was made before he was made; before he was made, I was already created. He ought to worship me&#x27;); LATIN ADAM-LITERATURE more broadly (Penitence of Adam Slavic recension); MERCED CYCLE in the Conflict of Adam and Eve (Dillmann 1853); QUR&#x27;AN Sura 7:12 (Iblis: &#x27;I am better than him: thou createdst me from fire, and him thou createdst from clay&#x27;). The Meqabyan parallel locates the argument in the Devil&#x27;s own mouth — the SELF-INCRIMINATING-PRIDE-SPEECH mode. Theological implication: pride is COGNITIVE-DISTORTION (false reasoning about created-priority) rather than merely volitional-disobedience.</p></aside>',
