        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>POST-FALL DIVINE JUDGMENT-PRONOUNCEMENT (vv. 22-25): God&#x27;s irrevocable verdict on the Devil. The verse parallels: GENESIS 3:14-15 (the curse-on-the-serpent — &#x27;I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel&#x27; — the Protoevangelium); EZEKIEL 28:16-19 (the king-of-Tyre / Satan-fall judgment-pronouncement — &#x27;I will cast thee as profane out of the mountain of God; I will destroy thee, O covering cherub, from the midst of the stones of fire&#x27;); ISAIAH 14:15 (Lucifer&#x27;s-fall — &#x27;thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit&#x27;); REVELATION 12:9 + 20:10 (the final-defeat). Meqabyan&#x27;s distinctive feature: the judgment is DELIVERED VIA THE DEVIL&#x27;S OWN PETITION (Ch 1 first-person speech) — the rebel arrests-and-condemns himself by his own argumentation. Tewahedo theology preserves this self-incrimination as the paradigm for unrepentant-sin (4:34 complete-repentance contrast).</p></aside>',
