        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>DIVINE-RESTORATION-OF-INHERITANCE — the verse&#x27;s promise: those whom the Devil could not deceive shall INHERIT his lost-glory. Direct parallels to the angelic-replacement doctrine: AUGUSTINE Enchiridion §29 (&#x27;the empty places of the city of God may be filled up by the elect of the human race&#x27;); ANSELM Cur Deus Homo I.16-18 (the most extended single treatment — the elect-fill-the-angelic-vacancies); GREGORY THE GREAT Homiliae in Evangelia 34 (the lost-drachma + humans-replace-the-fallen-tenth doctrine — see seed 3 Mq 4:8 &#x27;tenth tribe&#x27;); THOMAS AQUINAS Summa Theologiae I.23.7 (the doctrine formalized scholastically). The angelic-replacement doctrine is preserved in EOTC Mäṣḥafä Mälaʾek (Book of the Angels) and integrated into Tewahedo angelological catechesis. The verse establishes the SOTERIOLOGICAL TELOS for the entire 3 Mq theological-anthropology systematic (Chs 4-10): humans are designed-to-replace-the-fallen-tenth, fulfilled-through-grace + complete-repentance.</p></aside>',
