        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of human-cooperation-with-divine-mercy theme. The synergistic-soteriology theme is characteristic of EOTC tradition: divine-grace and human-cooperation work together; faith-without-works is incomplete (Jas 2:14-26 EOTC-canonical-reception); works-without-faith is presumptuous. The synergism-framework parallels: GREEK PATRISTIC TRADITION more broadly (Athanasius De Incarnatione 54 + Gregory of Nazianzus Or 30.21 + Cyril of Alexandria Commentary on John 15:1-8 — synergism-with-Christ-the-vine); EPHRAEM THE SYRIAN Hymns on Faith 5 + 8 (faith-and-knowledge synergism); JOHN CHRYSOSTOM Homilies on Romans 16 (the synergy of grace and free-will). The verse-position likely articulates the EOTC framework that complete-repentance (Ch 4:34) presupposes: divine-mercy + human-confession + human-weeping + human-non-return.</p></aside>',
