        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>ADAM-IMAGE-OF-GOD theology elaboration: the verse likely develops Adam&#x27;s CREATEDNESS IN THE IMAGE OF GOD as the basis for the Satan-refused-to-worship-Adam tradition (seed 1:15). The image-of-God reading parallels: GENESIS 1:26-27 (&#x27;let us make man in our image, after our likeness&#x27;); WISDOM 2:23 (&#x27;God created man to be immortal, and made him to be an image of his own eternity&#x27;); COLOSSIANS 1:15 (Christ-as-image-of-the-invisible-God); 2 CORINTHIANS 4:4 (Christ-as-image); IRENAEUS Adversus Haereses 5.16 (image-and-likeness distinction); ATHANASIUS De Incarnatione 3-13 (Christ-restores-the-image — γ.4.9 Athanasian arc anchor); GREGORY OF NYSSA De Hominis Opificio 4-5 (the most extended patristic image-theology). Tewahedo image-theology preserves the image-and-likeness distinction: Adam-as-image is INALIENABLE; Adam-as-likeness is LOST-AT-FALL-AND-RESTORED-IN-CHRIST. The verse anchors the THEOLOGICAL JUSTIFICATION for the angelic-veneration-of-Adam that triggered the Devil&#x27;s refusal.</p></aside>',
