        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Third Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan III)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>HOMILETIC-GENRE ANCHOR — likely development of FINAL-JUDGMENT-AND-REWARD theme. The final-judgment theme parallels: MATTHEW 25:31-46 (the sheep-and-goats judgment); REVELATION 20:11-15 (the great-white-throne — direct parallel to mq2 20:13 γ.4.8.C detail-wave); DANIEL 7:9-14 + 12:1-3 (the ancient-of-days + the resurrection-of-the-just-and-unjust); 4 EZRA 7:26-44 (the seven-day-judgment-cosmology — γ.4.4 Mäṣḥafä Hēnok parallels at γ.4.4.E arc-close); 1 ENOCH 22 (the four-chambers-of-Sheol doctrine). The trilogy&#x27;s THREE-FOLD JUDGMENT-PARALLEL — 1 Mq 36:45 (resurrection capstone tricolon) + 2 Mq 20:13 (judgment-throne formula Rev 20:11-15) + 3 Mq 9:5 (final-judgment-and-reward systematic-introduction) — establishes ECHOING-ESCHATOLOGY as a characteristic Mäqabyan structural-signature. Tewahedo eschatology preserves the three-fold judgment-echo as the canonical-systematic framework.</p></aside>',
